3\", \"b2b647169c633d36215dcec3936827bc0d27fb369c064bab2ac8dc8c535edc3f\", \"94f3b1d3dabbde57109e81cb83ddff97927cef9596e2056108e646fad9248da5\", \"4655db04f2a9e05ff6fc330b18cff97b3c74ef6519af82c3cc840bbdb9e30cb6\", \"ac10dd4ffea8a68a0c29544a3d20a60ea2213c04c95bc1d6c54fa864f92e1f07\", \"4a1bcb93b89ddf7d6dca52da1e2cd6d34e2728568ee57dbda29294bb43735f39\", \"ebd705c057d8c63efa8d32786e2839271d7a5df4a6e062223e7a2edb9bc41fd2\", \"75153e960649beb959dbb00cea1f9cdf846891bbe464b1306bd9ccc39c7dbcf4\", \"866c96c348547b4d56989dcf0a8b23d63a903c6fb67f0311b2ef36df20151897\", \"cfb5301091bfa2bd87467724f3e4d3736035a5ccef62e5142a311c78198c5dd7\", \"2bdd1e204b71a18a284699333d33269a3c27bb6537e5d0a695df79f58c7a57ee\", \"b4dd8a3dc58cd1abe478500a2021d48ac678475532308df895554c17019c726d\"],\n  \"reviewerType\": \"llm-vision-headless-cli\",\n  \"summary\": \"The Member Social Space screens render real, plausible community content in places (Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee, \\\"Can you bring the sign-in sheets before the meetup?\\\", \\\"Sponsored by Neighborhood Newsletter\\\", \\\"Safety note from moderator Alex, updated today at 10:30 AM\\\") and the ad-slot workflows do a genuinely good job of stating a no-fill reason. But the surface is dominated by acceptance-criteria prose rendered as UI copy — labels like \\\"Reply, read/unread, archive, mute, block, draft, or resend actions match the message state.\\\" and \\\"Sender, recipient or audience, timestamp, body, and delivery channel are visible.\\\" describe the screen instead of being the screen. Every \\\"complete\\\" screenshot clips its own confirmation banner behind the bottom nav (\\\"Banner no-fill recorded / No sponsored message is shown\\\" cut mid-line; \\\"and appeal/unblock option\\\" cut; \\\"continuation\\\" cut), so the one element that proves completion is the one element that is truncated. Most seriously, platform-message-stream is not distinctly evidenced: its action and complete screenshots are byte-identical to platform-messages-entry (hashes b2b6471… and 94f3b1d…), and its start screenshot shows connection-invite content instead. Overall: fail.\",\n  \"holisticQuestionAnswers\": [\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"context-state-legibility\",\n      \"question\": \"Across this community's workflows, is it always clear what workflow and what state (start/in-progress/complete) the user is looking at?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Partially. The action-state sheets are the strongest: each has a distinctly colored header naming the surface (\\\"Message thread\\\" on blue, \\\"Connection safety guard\\\" on maroon, \\\"Top banner slot\\\" on green, \\\"Sensitive ad decision\\\" on purple, \\\"Sponsored message details\\\" on brown), so workflow identity reads instantly. Start and complete states are much weaker. Several start screens open mid-scroll on a fragment (messages-entry begins with an orphaned line \\\"preserves read/unread receipt.\\\" under the app bar), and every complete screen truncates the confirmation chip that is supposed to signal completion. Worse, platform-message-stream cannot be told apart from platform-messages-entry at all — the same \\\"Message thread\\\" sheet and the same \\\"Community message thread / Message sent\\\" complete screen appear under both row IDs, and message-stream's start screen shows \\\"Member connection invite\\\" content.\",\n      \"score\": 42,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"platform-message-stream-action and platform-messages-entry-action are the identical 'Message thread' sheet showing 'Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee' and 'Can you bring the sign-in sheets before the meetup?' (same hash b2b6471…)\",\n        \"platform-message-stream-start shows the heading 'Member connection invite' with 'Invite body / Message: \\\"Want to coordinate the Saturday welcome table together?\\\"' and a 'Cancel invite' button — connection-invite content, not a message stream\",\n        \"platform-top-banner-no-fill-complete clips its green confirmation card at 'Banner no-fill recorded / No sponsored message is shown' mid-sentence behind the Home/Calendar/Admin/Messages bar\",\n        \"platform-messages-entry-start opens on the orphan fragment 'preserves read/unread receipt.' directly under the 'Member Social Space' app bar with no visible section heading\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-complete\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"copy-accuracy\",\n      \"question\": \"Does the displayed text read as real product copy about actual community content, or as generic/spec-derived placeholder prose?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Mixed, and the spec-derived half dominates the pixel area. Genuine product-sounding strings exist and are good: \\\"Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee, members of the same community.\\\", \\\"Can you bring the sign-in sheets before the meetup?\\\", \\\"Today 9:12 AM, expires in 7 days if unanswered.\\\", \\\"Safety note from moderator Alex, updated today at 10:30 AM.\\\", \\\"Sponsored by Neighborhood Newsletter.\\\" But sitting immediately beneath them are rows that are plainly restated acceptance criteria: \\\"Sender, recipient or audience, timestamp, body, and delivery channel are visible.\\\", \\\"Reply, read/unread, archive, mute, block, draft, or resend actions match the message state.\\\", \\\"Show sender, protected recipient, attempted invite body, disabled send option, safety reason, appeal/unblock option, and audit timestamp.\\\" A member would never be told what is \\\"visible\\\" on the screen they are already looking at. The minimized cards are worse — \\\"Connections\\\", \\\"Connection invite\\\" and \\\"Message stream rend…\\\" all carry the identical truncated subtitle \\\"Member communication stays scoped to the com…\\\", which reads as a filler string stamped across every card.\",\n      \"score\": 35,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"'Conversation state — Reply, read/unread, archive, mute, block, draft, or resend actions match the message state.' appears verbatim in the messages-entry, blocked-target, connections-entry and connection-invite action sheets\",\n        \"Three different cards on platform-messages-entry-start and platform-connections-entry-start share the byte-identical subtitle 'Member communication stays scoped to the com…'\",\n        \"'Sponsored-message controls — Review reserved slot behavior, disclosure, no-fill reason, entitlement, receipt, and restore option.' is a checklist of what to review, not copy for a member\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-action\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"actionability\",\n      \"question\": \"Are the available actions clear, and is it clear why disabled or hidden ones are unavailable?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No, in the safety and ad workflows. The blocked-target screens narrate controls that are not rendered: \\\"disabled send option ... appeal/unblock option\\\" appears in body text, but there is no visibly disabled Send control and no Appeal or Unblock button anywhere in the start, action, or complete screenshot — the user is told an appeal path exists and given no way to take it. The ad workflows are the same shape: \\\"manage-ad controls\\\", \\\"restore/manage action\\\", \\\"receipt link\\\" and \\\"dismiss, report, and manage-ad controls\\\" are all described in prose with no corresponding tappable control in frame. Where real buttons do exist they are clear and well labeled — \\\"Archive thread\\\", \\\"Reply\\\", \\\"Connect\\\", \\\"Send invite\\\", \\\"Cancel invite\\\", \\\"Send message\\\" — so the gap is specifically that the guard and monetization surfaces substitute description for affordance.\",\n      \"score\": 38,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"platform-blocked-target-start body reads 'disabled send option, safety reason, appeal/unblock option, and audit timestamp' while the screen contains no Send, Appeal, or Unblock control at all\",\n        \"platform-in-stream-ad-action lists 'dismiss, report, and manage-ad controls sit inside the stream' with no Dismiss or Report button rendered in the sheet\",\n        \"platform-top-banner-no-fill-action shows 'Ad-free account — ... receipt link, restore/manage action ...' as static text with no link or button\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-action\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"visual-quality\",\n      \"question\": \"Is the visual execution production-grade — no repeated generic shells, no clipping, no thin content, no contrast problems?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No. Four distinct visual defects recur. (1) Clipping at the bottom nav on every complete-state screen, cutting the confirmation text mid-word or mid-line. (2) The 'Messages' bottom-nav pill is sliced by the right screen edge on 10 of the 12 in-app screens, rendering as 'Messages' with the trailing pill missing. (3) Workflow hero titles are drawn in a saturated-on-dark tint that reads as disabled: 'Top banner no-fill' in dark green on navy, 'Sensitive page ad guard' in purple on navy, 'Sponsored stream message' in brown on navy, each with an even dimmer subtitle beneath. (4) The minimized cards are literally the same shell repeated — same icon, same 'Minimized' chip, same 'Tap for expanded view' + 'Community setting' pair, same truncated subtitle — stacked two and three deep. platform-connection-invite-start also ends in roughly a quarter-screen of empty navy below a collapsed 'Local package details' row.\",\n      \"score\": 33,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"platform-sensitive-no-fill-complete cuts the purple card at 'Sensitive no-fill recorded' with its body text entirely hidden behind the bottom nav\",\n        \"The 'Sponsored stream message' title on platform-in-stream-ad-start is rendered in a dark ochre/brown against the navy panel, noticeably lower contrast than the white 'In-stream placement' heading directly below it\",\n        \"platform-connection-invite-start shows a large empty dark region under the 'Local package details' disclosure row before the bottom nav\",\n        \"The 'Messages' nav pill is clipped by the right edge on messages-entry, blocked-target, connections-entry, message-stream, sensitive-no-fill start and in-stream-ad start screens\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-complete\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"workflow-scoping-correctness\",\n      \"question\": \"Does the content shown on each screen make sense for the workflow it is labelled with?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Not consistently. platform-message-stream is the clearest violation: its start screen is scrolled to connection-invite content ('Member connection invite', 'Invite body', 'Cancel invite'), and its action and complete screens are pixel-identical to platform-messages-entry's, so nothing in the evidence distinguishes a message stream from a single message thread. platform-messages-entry-start likewise shows mostly Connections and Connection invite cards rather than a messages inbox. platform-blocked-target-complete highlights the 'Calendar' tab in the bottom nav while displaying the Blocked connection guard, which is a navigation-scoping error — every other screen in the set highlights 'Home'. Where scoping is right it is clearly right: the ad workflows correctly separate a no-fill top banner, a sensitive-context suppression, and a filled in-stream placement with a named sponsor.\",\n      \"score\": 30,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"platform-blocked-target-complete highlights 'Calendar' in the bottom nav while the content area shows 'Blocked connection guard' and 'Blocked state confirmed'\",\n        \"platform-message-stream-start's dominant heading is 'Member connection invite' with 'Send a connection invite with sender, recipient, invite message body...'\",\n        \"platform-messages-entry-start's visible cards are titled 'Connections' and 'Connection invite', not a message list\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-complete\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screenReviews\": [\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This is supposed to be the entry point into messages, but the viewport opens mid-scroll on the orphan sentence 'preserves read/unread receipt.' with no owning heading above it, followed by an 'Archive thread' chip and a full-width 'Reply' pill that belong to a thread the user cannot see. Below that sit two identical card shells — 'Connections' and 'Connection invite' — each with the same 'Minimized' chip, the same 'Tap for expanded view' and 'Community setting' chips, and the exact same truncated subtitle 'Member communication stays scoped to the com…'. Nothing on screen names a messages inbox or shows a list of conversations, and the 'Messages' nav pill at bottom right is sliced off by the screen edge.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A messages entry point should open at the top of a real inbox: a 'Messages' heading, a list of conversations each showing correspondent name, message snippet, timestamp and unread state, and a clear primary action to open or start a thread.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Orphan text 'preserves read/unread receipt.' directly under the 'Member Social Space' app bar\", \"'Archive thread' chip and full-width 'Reply' pill with no visible thread context\", \"'Connections' and 'Connection invite' cards with identical 'Minimized' chip and identical truncated subtitle 'Member communication stays scoped to the com…'\", \"'Expand' + 'Connect' and 'Expand' + 'Send invite' button pairs\", \"'Messages' bottom-nav pill clipped by the right edge\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is it clear this is the start state of a messages-entry workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The topmost readable text is 'preserves read/unread receipt.' and the only headings are 'Connections' and 'Connection invite'\",\n          \"why\": \"No inbox heading, no conversation list, and the two visible cards are about connections rather than messages, so the workflow identity is not legible from the pixels.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are repeated generic card shells present?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Both cards show 'Minimized', 'Tap for expanded view', 'Community setting' and 'Member communication stays scoped to the com…'\",\n          \"why\": \"Two stacked cards differing only in title and one button label is the definition of a repeated generic shell.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"14113a2b76248a422a0cd2a9c89366daf0cf0db968ed9995e04135e78612f1a8\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The blue 'Message thread' sheet header with an X close is the strongest state signal in the whole set, and the top 'Conversation' card carries genuinely product-grade content: 'Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee, members of the same community.', 'Can you bring the sign-in sheets before the meetup?', 'Today 9:12 AM, unread until opened.' The sheet then undermines itself twice. First, 'Actions — Reply, mute, archive, or block remain available.' is prose about buttons rather than the buttons themselves; no Reply, Mute, Archive or Block control is rendered in this sheet. Second, the 'Thread actions' card below repeats the very same 'Sender and recipient / Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee' and 'Message body / Can you bring the sign-in sheets before the' rows already shown above, so the user reads the same conversation facts twice on one screen.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"An opened thread should show the message bubbles themselves plus real tappable Reply / Mute / Archive / Block controls, with no duplicated restatement of sender and body further down the sheet.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Blue sheet header 'Message thread' with X close\", \"'Sender and recipient — Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee, members of the same community.'\", \"'Timestamp — Today 9:12 AM, unread until opened.'\", \"'Actions — Reply, mute, archive, or block remain available.' with no corresponding buttons\", \"'Thread actions' card repeats 'Sender and recipient' and 'Message body' verbatim\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy describe real community content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Can you bring the sign-in sheets before the meetup?'\",\n          \"why\": \"That line is plausible member-to-member copy tied to a real community activity, and it is the best copy on the screen.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are the stated actions actionable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Reply, mute, archive, or block remain available.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The sentence asserts availability but no Reply/Mute/Archive/Block affordance is drawn, so the user cannot act on any of them from this sheet.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"b2b647169c633d36215dcec3936827bc0d27fb369c064bab2ac8dc8c535edc3f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The completion signal here is the blue 'Message sent' card, and it is the one thing that reads correctly as a terminal state. But its body — 'The thread shows the sent message, receiver read status, timestamp, reply option, receipt history, and archive/block controls.' — is a description of a thread view rather than the thread view, and it directly contradicts the card above it, which still says 'Today 9:12 AM, unread until opened.' and 'Reply, mute, archive, or block remain available.' A user reading top to bottom sees an unread inbound message and a 'Message sent' confirmation on the same screen with no reconciliation. The heading 'Community message thread' with its sub-line listing 'sender, recipient, timestamp, message preview, unread receipt, reply option, mute, and archive controls' is again spec text, and the card below 'Message sent' is cut off by the bottom nav.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A completed send should show the sent message in the thread with a real delivery/read indicator and a timestamp, not a paragraph enumerating what the thread contains alongside a stale 'unread until opened' card.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'Message sent' card on blue with checkmark-style message icon\", \"Conflicting text 'Today 9:12 AM, unread until opened.' still visible above it\", \"Heading 'Community message thread' with an enumerated feature list as its subtitle\", \"A further card begins below 'Message sent' and is clipped by the bottom nav\", \"'Home' tab highlighted in bottom nav\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the complete state unambiguous?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Message sent — The thread shows the sent message, receiver read status, timestamp...'\",\n          \"why\": \"The confirmation is present but sits directly beneath 'unread until opened', so the screen simultaneously asserts an unread inbound message and a completed send.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"94f3b1d3dabbde57109e81cb83ddff97927cef9596e2056108e646fad9248da5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Content-wise this is one of the better screens: 'Maya Chen attempted to invite Jordan Lee; Jordan remains protected by an active block.', the quoted attempt 'Join my community circle for Saturday event planning.', and 'Safety note from moderator Alex, updated today at 10:30 AM.' all read like real moderation records, and the shield-icon 'Receiver protection' row states the outcome plainly. The failure is actionability: the 'Blocked connection guard' body explicitly promises 'disabled send option, safety reason, appeal/unblock option, and audit timestamp', yet the screen renders no disabled Send control and no Appeal or Unblock affordance anywhere — the promised remedy path is described and then withheld. The 'Conversation actions' card that follows is also pure narration ('The member cannot send the invite while the block is active') rather than a visibly greyed-out button that would make the constraint self-evident.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A blocked-target guard should render the Send control in a visibly disabled state with an inline reason, plus a real 'Request unblock' or 'Appeal' button, next to the moderator safety note and audit timestamp.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'Sender and protected recipient — Maya Chen attempted to invite Jordan Lee; Jordan remains protected by an active block.'\", \"'Attempted invite body — Invite text: \\\"Join my community circle for Saturday event planning.\\\"'\", \"'Community safety record — Safety note from moderator Alex, updated today at 10:30 AM.'\", \"Shield icon 'Receiver protection — The protected member does not receive unsafe contact.'\", \"No disabled Send button and no appeal/unblock control anywhere on screen\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is it clear why the blocked action is unavailable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'The member cannot send the invite while the block is active; the attempted message body stays in audit, not in Jordan's inbox.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The reason is stated well in prose, but with no disabled control on screen the user has nothing to attach that reason to and no path to appeal.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"6c2a9922569b9f447a13b4eb50f60032e4fbd63f2119c76a187d6ac7b663bda7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The maroon 'Connection safety guard' header is an excellent state cue — the colour shift from the blue message sheets immediately tells the user they are in a protective/blocked context rather than an ordinary thread, and the tinted card backgrounds carry it through consistently. The problem is the lower half: the 'Thread actions' card is the same generic block used on the messages sheet, opening with 'Read sender, body, timestamp, and choose reply, mute, archive, or block.' and 'Conversation state — Reply, read/unread, archive, mute, block, draft, or resend actions match the message state.' None of that is true here — this is a blocked invite where reply and resend are precisely what is not allowed. It then re-lists 'Sender and protected recipient' and begins 'Attempted invite body' a second time at the clipped bottom edge, duplicating what the card above already said.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The guard sheet should show block-specific actions (view safety note, request unblock, report) rather than a reused generic thread-actions block that advertises reply/resend on a conversation where they are prohibited.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Maroon sheet header 'Connection safety guard' with X close\", \"Maroon-tinted 'Conversation' card with 'Receiver protection' shield row\", \"'Thread actions — Read sender, body, timestamp, and choose reply, mute, archive, or block.'\", \"'Conversation state — Reply, read/unread, archive, mute, block, draft, or resend actions match the message state.'\", \"'Sender and protected recipient' repeated lower in the sheet; 'Attempted invite body' clipped at the bottom edge\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the content make sense for a blocked-target workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'choose reply, mute, archive, or block' appearing inside the 'Connection safety guard' sheet\",\n          \"why\": \"Offering reply and resend inside a guard whose whole premise is that sending is blocked is internally contradictory scoping.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the state visually legible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Maroon header bar reading 'Connection safety guard'\",\n          \"why\": \"The distinct colour and title make the protective state legible at a glance, which is the screen's real strength.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"24f84f8d9e42dc5bfbbe30082d9ef3da3c8d14254ea653c0bf27f4eaf6aa5df3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Two defects here, one of them a scoping error unique to this screen: the bottom navigation highlights the 'Calendar' pill in solid blue while the content area shows 'Blocked connection guard' and 'Blocked state confirmed' — every other screen in this set highlights 'Home', so the nav is asserting the user is in Calendar while reading a messaging safety record. Separately, the maroon 'Blocked state confirmed' card, which is the entire completion signal, is truncated mid-sentence at 'audit timestamp, and appeal/unblock option' by the bottom nav bar, so the confirmation the screen exists to deliver is the text that gets cut. The upper 'Conversation' card content ('Jordan remains protected by an active block', moderator Alex's note at 10:30 AM) remains accurate and well written.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A confirmed-block completion should keep the 'Blocked state confirmed' card fully visible above the nav, with the correct nav tab active, and expose the appeal/unblock option it names as a real control.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'Calendar' pill highlighted in solid blue in the bottom nav on a messaging/safety screen\", \"Maroon 'Blocked state confirmed' card clipped mid-line at 'and appeal/unblock option'\", \"'Blocked connection guard' heading with the enumerated-requirements subtitle\", \"'Community safety record — Safety note from moderator Alex, updated today at 10:30 AM.'\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completion state fully visible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'The community safety record shows sender, protected recipient, attempted body, disabled action, audit timestamp, and appeal/unblock option' cut off by the nav bar\",\n          \"why\": \"The confirmation card is clipped by the bottom navigation, so the terminal-state message cannot be read in full.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the navigation state match the content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Solid blue 'Calendar' pill with white calendar icon\",\n          \"why\": \"Calendar is highlighted while a blocked-connection guard is displayed, contradicting every other screen in the set which highlights Home.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"fed5ecc6c847fc05f1b2d7f0f6f8782219aa03fc7201c1e018952146be65136d\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This is the most successful screen in the set on substance: 'No sponsored message right now' is honest, member-facing copy, and 'Reason — No fill: no eligible sponsor for this community moment.' plus 'No impression — No impression/click is recorded because the slot is not filled.' explain the empty slot in terms a member can actually understand, with the reserved-space rationale spelled out under 'Layout'. The visual execution is what falls short: the hero title 'Top banner no-fill' and its subtitle 'Show a clear no-sponsored-message state with reserved space, disclosure, and no overlap.' are rendered in a dark desaturated green against the navy panel, low enough in contrast that the whole header block reads as greyed-out/disabled next to the crisp white 'Ad slot state' heading immediately below. The subtitle is also spec phrasing ('Show a clear... state') rather than product voice.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"Same no-fill explanation, but with the workflow title in a legible on-dark tint and a member-facing subtitle instead of a 'Show a clear ... state' requirement sentence.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'In-focus product surface' bar with 'Expand' affordance at top\", \"Hero title 'Top banner no-fill' in dark green on navy with a dimmer green subtitle\", \"'No sponsored message right now' with slashed-rectangle icon\", \"'Reason — No fill: no eligible sponsor for this community moment.'\", \"'Layout — Reserved space prevents overlap, crowding, and content jumps.'\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the empty/no-fill state explained rather than just blank?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'No fill: no eligible sponsor for this community moment.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The slot states both that it is empty and why, and confirms no impression was recorded — this is the correct treatment for an empty state.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the title legible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Top banner no-fill' drawn in dark green over the dark navy card\",\n          \"why\": \"The title and subtitle sit at markedly lower contrast than surrounding white text, reading as disabled rather than as the screen's heading.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"c7a31706952e380d6cd54a92da06852c147d046b2772ca2f41c5ca3bac3515aa\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The green 'Top banner slot' sheet is well themed and the 'Ad slot state' card repeats the four clear rows — Reserved placement, Reason, No impression, Layout — at full contrast on green, which is much more readable than the start screen's tinted hero. The lower 'Sponsored-message controls' card is where it breaks down: its subtitle 'Review reserved slot behavior, disclosure, no-fill reason, entitlement, receipt, and restore option.' is an instruction to a reviewer, not copy for a member, and both rows beneath it are inventories of things that are supposed to be visible rather than the things themselves — 'Ad-free account — Entitlement scope, renewal or expiry, receipt link, restore/manage action, and affected ad slots are visible.' names a receipt link and a restore action, neither of which is rendered as a tappable element. There is no actual entitlement status, no expiry date, and no receipt on screen.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The controls card should show the member's real ad-free entitlement state (active/expired plus a date), a tappable receipt link, and a Restore purchase button — not a sentence asserting those items are visible.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Green sheet header 'Top banner slot' with X close\", \"'No sponsored message right now' card at full contrast\", \"'Sponsored-message controls' with subtitle 'Review reserved slot behavior, disclosure, no-fill reason, entitlement, receipt, and restore option.'\", \"'Ad-free account — Entitlement scope, renewal or expiry, receipt link, restore/manage action, and affected ad slots are visible.'\", \"'Receipt or settlement — Payment receipt, settlement ID, utility allocation, audit status, correction, and rollback path remain visible where applicable.'\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the entitlement section show real data?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Entitlement scope, renewal or expiry, receipt link, restore/manage action, and affected ad slots are visible.'\",\n          \"why\": \"It lists the fields that should be present instead of presenting any of them — no scope, no date, no receipt link is actually rendered.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"ba4bca20cbad8906f0b2e3e01f8a8ecf626a6b5ad5286def481e1feae149514d\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The completion evidence is the green 'Banner no-fill recorded' card at the bottom, and it is clipped mid-second-line by the bottom nav — 'No sponsored message is shown' is cut off with its descender row half-drawn behind the nav bar, so the only text that distinguishes this screen from the start state is the text that is truncated. Everything above it is a verbatim re-render of the start screen: same dark-green 'Top banner no-fill' hero at the same low contrast, same 'Ad slot state' card with the same four rows. A user comparing start and complete would see an essentially identical screen plus a half-visible green strip.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The 'Banner no-fill recorded' confirmation should be fully visible above the bottom nav, ideally anchored or scrolled into view, and should carry a concrete detail (timestamp or slot ID) that distinguishes it from the pre-action state.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Green 'Banner no-fill recorded' card clipped at 'No sponsored message is shown'\", \"Hero 'Top banner no-fill' still rendered in low-contrast dark green\", \"'Ad slot state' card identical to the start screen's\", \"'Home' highlighted in bottom nav\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can the user tell this is the completed state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Banner no-fill recorded' visible but its body 'No sponsored message is shown' cut by the nav bar\",\n          \"why\": \"The distinguishing confirmation is present but partially occluded, and the rest of the screen is identical to the start state.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"8903d29c88ee7f89bd0e9b4b261b0e145f9c9537187e77d7ae2342dc72529917\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The screen opens mid-scroll on a heading that is itself clipped — only the descenders of 'Conversation actions' are visible above the body text 'Recipient sees the invite text, sender, timestamp, mutual community, accept, decline, block, and thread-continuation options.' That sentence is a requirements list, not something you would show a member. Below it are two more identical minimized shells, 'Connection invite' and a title truncated to 'Message stream rend…', both carrying the same 'Member communication stays scoped to the com…' subtitle and the same 'Tap for expanded view' / 'Community setting' chip pair. For a connections entry point there is no list of connections, no pending-request count, and no member names anywhere on screen — only 'Cancel invite', 'Connect', 'Expand' and 'Send invite' buttons floating without subjects.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A connections entry should list actual connections and pending requests with member names and avatars, a pending count, and clear Accept/Decline actions per row.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Clipped 'Conversation actions' heading at the top of the scroll viewport\", \"'Recipient sees the invite text, sender, timestamp, mutual community, accept, decline, block, and thread-continuation options.'\", \"'Cancel invite' chip and full-width 'Connect' pill\", \"Card titled 'Message stream rend…' truncated mid-word\", \"Two cards sharing the subtitle 'Member communication stays scoped to the com…'\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does this look like a connections list?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"No member names appear; the only headings are 'Connection invite' and 'Message stream rend…'\",\n          \"why\": \"A connections entry point with zero named connections and zero pending requests gives the user nothing to act on.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is any text clipped?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Message stream rend…' and the partially cut 'Conversation actions' heading\",\n          \"why\": \"Both a card title and a section heading are truncated in the same viewport.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"07a2dc129317ac156414407a1b0f65091663eee21e3edeb73a163924adea432b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The blue 'Connections inbox' sheet header names the surface clearly and the conversation card is good product copy: 'Maya Chen invites Jordan Lee to connect inside the community.', 'Message: \\\"Want to coordinate the Saturday welcome table together?\\\"', and the genuinely useful 'Today 9:12 AM, expires in 7 days if unanswered.' The 'Accepted' row with its check icon states the outcome. But no Accept or Decline button exists anywhere in the sheet even though the state is 'Accepted' — the user cannot see what they pressed or what they could press. The 'Thread actions' card underneath is the same reused generic block seen on the message and blocked-target sheets ('Reply, read/unread, archive, mute, block, draft, or resend actions match the message state.') and then re-lists 'Sender and recipient' and 'Invite body' a second time, so the sheet ends by repeating its own opening card.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A connections inbox sheet should render Accept and Decline as real buttons (or show the accepted state as a resolved chip with the acceptance time), without a duplicated restatement of the invite below.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Blue sheet header 'Connections inbox' with X close\", \"'Today 9:12 AM, expires in 7 days if unanswered.'\", \"Check-icon row 'Accepted — Accepted invites open a thread and connection history.'\", \"'Thread actions' generic block reused verbatim from the message-thread sheet\", \"'Sender and recipient' and 'Invite body' repeated lower in the sheet\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the invite content real-sounding?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Want to coordinate the Saturday welcome table together?'\",\n          \"why\": \"It names a specific community activity and reads as something one member would actually write to another.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are Accept/Decline actionable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Accepted invites open a thread and connection history.' with no Accept or Decline control rendered\",\n          \"why\": \"The accept/decline decision is described but not offered, and the reused 'Thread actions' block advertises reply/resend instead.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"372930b369dc20498695a08cbec5abd0ef3e653734d67deee7ada688766364db\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The blue 'Connection invite sent' card gives a real completion signal and the heading 'Connections inbox' names the surface, but the card is clipped by the bottom nav mid-word — the last visible line reads 'state, cancel option, and inbox' with 'continuation' sheared off. Its body is also an inventory ('The invite shows sender, recipient, message body, timestamp, accept/decline state, cancel option, and inbox continuation') rather than a confirmation a member would read, and it names a 'cancel option' that is not rendered as a control on this screen. The 'Connections inbox' subtitle beneath the heading — 'Manage connection requests with sender, message body, timestamp, mutual community, accept/decline choices, and blocked-contact status.' — is the same requirements-list voice.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A sent-invite confirmation should read as a short member-facing statement ('Invite sent to Jordan Lee · expires in 7 days') with a working Cancel invite action, fully visible above the nav bar.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Blue 'Connection invite sent' card clipped at 'state, cancel option, and inbox continuation'\", \"Heading 'Connections inbox' with an enumerated-requirements subtitle\", \"'Accepted' row still shown above the sent confirmation\", \"'Home' highlighted in bottom nav\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completion confirmation fully readable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'...accept/decline state, cancel option, and inbox continuation' cut mid-word by the nav bar\",\n          \"why\": \"The terminal-state card is truncated, so the completion message cannot be read in full.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"20790b355656fcf2532af4524f49a4cfe77c8b387f762be0a8433e5ded15cc18\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This row is labelled as the start of the message-stream workflow, but nothing on screen concerns a message stream. The dominant heading is 'Member connection invite', the visible content is the connection-invite conversation card ('Maya Chen invites Jordan Lee to connect inside the community.', 'Want to coordinate the Saturday welcome table together?', 'expires in 7 days if unanswered'), the state row reads 'Accepted', and the only button is 'Cancel invite'. It is effectively the connection-invite screen scrolled to a different offset. There is no stream, no ordered list of messages, no sender rotation, and no indication of stream length or position — a user landing here would believe they are in the invite flow.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A message-stream start should show an actual ordered stream of community messages — multiple entries from different senders with timestamps and read state — headed by a stream title, not a single connection invite.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Heading 'Member connection invite' with subtitle 'Send a connection invite with sender, recipient, invite message body, timestamp, accept/decline option, and inbox state.'\", \"'Invite body — Message: \\\"Want to coordinate the Saturday welcome table together?\\\"'\", \"Check-icon 'Accepted' row\", \"'Conversation actions' card ending in a 'Cancel invite' chip\", \"No stream, list, or multi-message content anywhere on screen\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the screen show the workflow it is labelled with?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The largest heading on screen reads 'Member connection invite'\",\n          \"why\": \"Connection-invite content is rendered under the message-stream row, so the evidence does not demonstrate the message-stream workflow at all.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"6090b19e04bb5c220efdbc3a1abd526ee7547d793417d1a59d825a62db6b78a3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This screenshot is byte-identical to the platform-messages-entry action screenshot (both hash b2b647169c63…): the same blue 'Message thread' header, the same single conversation 'Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee' with 'Can you bring the sign-in sheets before the meetup?' at 'Today 9:12 AM, unread until opened.', and the same duplicated 'Thread actions' block. A message stream and a single message thread are different surfaces — a stream should show many messages in sequence — yet the evidence for the two workflows is literally the same pixels, so this row demonstrates nothing specific to message-stream rendering. On its own merits the sheet also repeats 'Sender and recipient / Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee' and 'Message body' a second time in the lower card.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The message-stream action state should show a scrolling stream of multiple distinct messages with senders, timestamps and read markers — visibly different from a one-message thread sheet.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Identical to the messages-entry action screenshot (shared hash b2b647169c63…)\", \"Blue 'Message thread' header with X close\", \"Single conversation: 'Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee' / 'Can you bring the sign-in sheets before the meetup?'\", \"'Thread actions' block repeating sender and body rows already shown above\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is this screen distinguishable from the messages-entry action screen?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Both screens show 'Message thread' with 'Today 9:12 AM, unread until opened.' and share hash b2b647169c63…\",\n          \"why\": \"They are the same image, so no message-stream-specific behaviour is evidenced.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"b2b647169c633d36215dcec3936827bc0d27fb369c064bab2ac8dc8c535edc3f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Also byte-identical to the platform-messages-entry complete screenshot (both hash 94f3b1d3dabb…) — same 'Community message thread' heading, same blue 'Message sent' card, same stale 'Today 9:12 AM, unread until opened.' row above it. As message-stream evidence it is void: a completed stream render would show the stream populated with several messages, not a single sent-message confirmation borrowed from another workflow. The internal contradiction carries over too — 'unread until opened' and 'Message sent' coexist with no reconciliation, and the card below 'Message sent' is cut off by the bottom nav.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A completed message-stream render should show the fully populated stream with multiple messages in order and a clear 'you are caught up'/end-of-stream marker, distinct from the messages-entry send confirmation.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Identical to the messages-entry complete screenshot (shared hash 94f3b1d3dabb…)\", \"Heading 'Community message thread'\", \"Blue 'Message sent' card with clipped card beginning below it\", \"'Today 9:12 AM, unread until opened.' still displayed above the sent confirmation\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does this evidence a completed message stream?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Message sent — The thread shows the sent message, receiver read status...' on an image shared with messages-entry-complete\",\n          \"why\": \"It reuses the messages-entry completion screen verbatim and shows a single message, not a stream.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"94f3b1d3dabbde57109e81cb83ddff97927cef9596e2056108e646fad9248da5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The card at the top is titled 'Sensitive page ad sta…' — truncated mid-word in a card whose right side is occupied by a 'Minimized' chip — and its subtitle is likewise cut at 'Ad slot disclosure shows a no-fill result with no spon…'. Underneath, a blue 'Messages and connections' banner with the generic line 'Member communication and relationship controls.' sits between the ad card and an 'In-focus product surface' bar, then the screen drops into the same 'Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee' conversation card seen in three other workflows. The result is that the sensitive-context ad suppression this row is meant to demonstrate is only visible as a truncated title and a 'Start sensitive page ad status' button; the actual suppression reason is nowhere in frame.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The start state should lead with the sensitive-context notice and its suppression reason at full width, untruncated, rather than a clipped card title above unrelated conversation content.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Card title truncated to 'Sensitive page ad sta…'\", \"Subtitle truncated to 'Ad slot disclosure shows a no-fill result with no spon…'\", \"Buttons 'Tap for expanded view', 'Ad placement', 'Expand', 'Start sensitive page ad status'\", \"Blue banner 'Messages and connections — Member communication and relationship controls.'\", \"'Conversation' card with 'Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee' and 'Can you bring the sign-in sheets before the meetup?' below\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the sensitive-context suppression legible on this screen?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Only 'Sensitive page ad sta…' and 'no-fill result with no spon…' are visible, both truncated\",\n          \"why\": \"The reason for suppression never appears in frame, so the workflow's central point is not shown.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the copy specific to this community?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Member communication and relationship controls.'\",\n          \"why\": \"That banner subtitle is a generic category description with no community-specific content.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"4655db04f2a9e05ff6fc330b18cff97b3c74ef6519af82c3cc840bbdb9e30cb6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The purple 'Sensitive ad decision' sheet is the clearest articulation of this workflow anywhere in the set: 'Sensitive context — Care/protected content suppresses ad targeting and click tracking.' and 'Reason — No fill: sensitive context.' together tell a member exactly why the slot is empty and reassure them that no click tracking occurred, which is genuinely good privacy copy. The distinct purple theming also separates it cleanly from the green top-banner sheet. The weakness is the second card: 'Sponsored-message controls' repeats the identical 'Ad-free account' and 'Receipt or settlement' rows verbatim from the top-banner sheet, listing fields that 'are visible' and 'remain visible where applicable' without rendering any of them, and then begins repeating 'Sensitive context' a third time at the clipped bottom edge.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"Keep the sensitive-context explanation as-is and replace the reused controls card with the member's actual entitlement and receipt data, or omit it on a sensitive-context screen where it is not relevant.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Purple sheet header 'Sensitive ad decision' with X close\", \"'Sensitive context — Care/protected content suppresses ad targeting and click tracking.'\", \"'Reason — No fill: sensitive context.'\", \"'Sponsored-message controls' card identical to the one on the top-banner sheet\", \"'Sensitive context' beginning to repeat at the clipped bottom of the sheet\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the screen explain why no ad is shown?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'No fill: sensitive context.' alongside 'suppresses ad targeting and click tracking'\",\n          \"why\": \"The reason is stated in plain, member-comprehensible terms and paired with a privacy assurance — the strongest copy in the review.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"ac10dd4ffea8a68a0c29544a3d20a60ea2213c04c95bc1d6c54fa864f92e1f07\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The hero 'Sensitive page ad guard' is rendered in a muted purple on the navy panel with an even fainter purple subtitle ('Show the member why ads are suppressed, preserve layout, and avoid leaking protected context.'), so the screen's own title is the least legible text on it — and that subtitle is a requirement statement rather than product copy. The completion marker, the purple 'Sensitive no-fill recorded' card, is clipped so severely by the bottom nav that only its title row and shield icon are visible with no body text at all. Everything above it duplicates the action sheet's 'Ad slot state' card, so the recorded-completion distinction rests entirely on a card the user can barely see.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The 'Sensitive no-fill recorded' confirmation should be fully in view with its body text, and the workflow title should be rendered at readable contrast against the dark panel.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Hero title 'Sensitive page ad guard' in low-contrast purple on navy\", \"Subtitle 'Show the member why ads are suppressed, preserve layout, and avoid leaking protected context.' fainter still\", \"Purple 'Sensitive no-fill recorded' card clipped to its title row only\", \"'Ad slot state' card duplicating the action sheet's rows\", \"'Home' highlighted in bottom nav\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completion state visible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Sensitive no-fill recorded' appears with zero body text before the nav bar cuts it off\",\n          \"why\": \"Only the title of the confirmation card survives the clip, leaving the completion essentially unexplained.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"4a1bcb93b89ddf7d6dca52da1e2cd6d34e2728568ee57dbda29294bb43735f39\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The top of the viewport is clipped mid-heading ('Conversation actions' is sheared to its descenders) and the visible body — 'Recipient sees the invite text, sender, timestamp, mutual community, accept, decline, block, and thread-continuation options.' — narrates the recipient's experience rather than showing the sender theirs. A 'Send invite' pill and a 'Cancel invite' chip both appear with no visible invite draft or recipient name attached. Below that is another duplicate shell card, 'Message stream rend…' (title truncated), with the recycled subtitle 'Member communication stays scoped to the com…'. The bottom third of the screen is a collapsed 'Local package details' row followed by roughly a quarter-screen of empty navy — thin, unfinished content where an invite composer or recipient picker should be.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"An invite start should show a composer: recipient selection, the invite message field, mutual-community context, and a single clear Send invite action — with no dead vertical space.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Clipped 'Conversation actions' heading at the top of the viewport\", \"Full-width 'Send invite' pill and 'Cancel invite' chip with no named recipient\", \"Card titled 'Message stream rend…' truncated, subtitle 'Member communication stays scoped to the com…'\", \"Collapsed 'Local package details' row with chevron\", \"Large empty dark region between that row and the bottom nav\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is there visible empty or thin content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Roughly a quarter of the screen below 'Local package details' is blank navy\",\n          \"why\": \"A start state ending in a large empty region reads as unfinished rather than as an intentional composer surface.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the primary action clear?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Send invite' and 'Cancel invite' both present with no recipient or draft shown\",\n          \"why\": \"Two opposing invite actions appear with no subject, so it is unclear what would be sent or cancelled.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"ebd705c057d8c63efa8d32786e2839271d7a5df4a6e062223e7a2edb9bc41fd2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The blue 'Connection invite' sheet reads well at the top: named parties ('Maya Chen invites Jordan Lee to connect inside the community.'), a real invite message ('Want to coordinate the Saturday welcome table together?'), and an expiry that carries actual product logic ('Today 9:12 AM, expires in 7 days if unanswered.'). The 'Accepted' row states the outcome. Below that the sheet degrades into the same recycled 'Thread actions' block used on the message-thread and connections-inbox sheets — 'Read sender, body, timestamp, and choose reply, mute, archive, or block.' — which is wrong for an invite (an invite is accepted or declined, not muted or archived) — and then re-renders 'Sender and recipient' and 'Invite body' a second time, so the bottom half of the sheet is a duplicate of the top half wrapped in an inapplicable action vocabulary.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The invite sheet should offer Accept / Decline / Block as real controls appropriate to an invite, and drop the duplicated restatement of sender and invite body.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Blue sheet header 'Connection invite' with X close\", \"'Maya Chen invites Jordan Lee to connect inside the community.'\", \"'Today 9:12 AM, expires in 7 days if unanswered.'\", \"'Thread actions — Read sender, body, timestamp, and choose reply, mute, archive, or block.'\", \"'Sender and recipient' and 'Invite body' repeated in the lower card\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Do the offered actions fit a connection invite?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'choose reply, mute, archive, or block' shown inside the 'Connection invite' sheet\",\n          \"why\": \"Reply/mute/archive are thread verbs, not invite verbs; accept and decline — the actions this workflow needs — are never offered as controls.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"75153e960649beb959dbb00cea1f9cdf846891bbe464b1306bd9ccc39c7dbcf4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The blue 'Connection invite sent' card with its person-plus icon is a legible completion marker and the heading 'Member connection invite' names the workflow correctly — this is the better of the two invite-completion screens. It still clips: the card's last visible line is 'state, cancel option, and inbox' with 'continuation' cut by the bottom nav. And the card's content contradicts the card above it, which shows a check-icon 'Accepted' row — the screen simultaneously reports that the invite was just sent and that it has already been accepted. The subtitle 'Send a connection invite with sender, recipient, invite message body, timestamp, accept/decline option, and inbox state.' is again requirement phrasing.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A sent-invite completion should show one coherent state — sent and pending, with expiry and a Cancel action — not a 'sent' confirmation stacked on an 'Accepted' row, and it should not be clipped by the nav bar.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Blue 'Connection invite sent' card with person-plus icon, clipped at 'and inbox continuation'\", \"Check-icon 'Accepted — Accepted invites open a thread and connection history.' shown above it\", \"Heading 'Member connection invite' with enumerated-requirements subtitle\", \"'Today 9:12 AM, expires in 7 days if unanswered.'\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the terminal state internally consistent?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Accepted' row directly above 'Connection invite sent'\",\n          \"why\": \"Sent-and-pending and already-accepted are mutually exclusive states shown together on one screen.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"866c96c348547b4d56989dcf0a8b23d63a903c6fb67f0311b2ef36df20151897\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This is the best-evidenced ad workflow: 'Sponsored by Neighborhood Newsletter' appears as an explicit disclosure both as the card title and again under a storefront-icon 'Sponsor' row, 'Reason — Filled ad: eligible community stream placement.' explains why this slot is filled where sibling screens explain why theirs are empty, and 'Impression recorded — Impression is recorded with sponsor disclosure and audit trail.' correctly contrasts with the no-fill screens' 'No impression'. Two problems. The hero 'Sponsored stream message' is drawn in dark ochre on navy at clearly lower contrast than the white 'In-stream placement' heading below it, and its subtitle 'Show sponsor, disclosure, message copy, impression state, and dismiss/report alternatives.' is a requirements sentence. More substantively, there is no sponsored creative — no headline, no ad body copy, no image — and no Dismiss or Report control, despite the card asserting 'dismiss, report, and manage-ad controls sit inside the stream'.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A filled in-stream ad should render the actual sponsored creative (headline plus body) under the 'Sponsored by' disclosure, with working Dismiss, Report and Manage-ad controls in the card.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'In-focus product surface' bar with 'Expand'\", \"Hero 'Sponsored stream message' in dark ochre on navy with dimmer subtitle\", \"'Sponsored by Neighborhood Newsletter' as card title and again in the 'Sponsor' row\", \"'Reason — Filled ad: eligible community stream placement.'\", \"'Impression recorded — Impression is recorded with sponsor disclosure and audit trail.'\", \"No ad creative copy and no Dismiss/Report buttons\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the sponsorship disclosed clearly?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Sponsored by Neighborhood Newsletter' appears twice, once as the card title\",\n          \"why\": \"The disclosure is prominent and names a specific, plausible community sponsor — this is done correctly.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the advertised content present?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Disclosure, sponsor creative, impression state, dismiss, report, and manage-ad controls sit inside the stream.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The card describes a sponsor creative and controls that are not rendered; there is no ad copy or dismiss affordance on screen.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"cfb5301091bfa2bd87467724f3e4d3736035a5ccef62e5142a311c78198c5dd7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The brown 'Sponsored message details' sheet is consistently themed and the 'In-stream placement' card carries the four ad rows at good contrast — Sponsor, Reason ('Filled ad: eligible community stream placement.'), Impression recorded, and Layout. But this detail sheet, which exists precisely so a member can inspect and manage a sponsored message, offers no management: the 'Sponsored-message controls' card below is the identical block reused from the top-banner and sensitive sheets, with 'Ad-free account — Entitlement scope, renewal or expiry, receipt link, restore/manage action, and affected ad slots are visible.' and 'Receipt or settlement — Payment receipt, settlement ID, utility allocation, audit status, correction, and rollback path remain visible where applicable.' Neither renders a value or a control, and 'Sponsor' begins repeating a third time at the clipped bottom edge.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The sponsored-message detail sheet should expose Why am I seeing this, Hide this ad, Report ad, and a real ad-free entitlement status with a receipt link — not a reused card listing fields that are supposed to be visible.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Brown sheet header 'Sponsored message details' with X close\", \"'Sponsor — Disclosure: Sponsored by Neighborhood Newsletter.'\", \"'Impression recorded — Impression is recorded with sponsor disclosure and audit trail.'\", \"'Sponsored-message controls' card identical to the top-banner and sensitive sheets\", \"'Sponsor' row beginning to repeat at the clipped bottom of the sheet\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can the member manage this sponsored message from the detail sheet?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'restore/manage action, and affected ad slots are visible.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The only management language on the sheet is a sentence claiming controls are visible; no hide, report, or manage control is drawn.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"2bdd1e204b71a18a284699333d33269a3c27bb6537e5d0a695df79f58c7a57ee\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The completion state is indicated only by a brown strip peeking above the bottom nav below the 'In-stream placement' card — its title and body are entirely hidden, so nothing readable on this screen distinguishes it from the in-stream-ad start state. Above that strip the content is a pixel-level repeat of the start screen: same low-contrast ochre 'Sponsored stream message' hero, same 'Sponsored by Neighborhood Newsletter' card, same Sponsor / Reason / Impression recorded / Layout rows. The disclosure and impression copy remain correct and specific, but as evidence of a completed state this screen shows a fully occluded confirmation.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The completion confirmation (e.g. 'Sponsored impression recorded' with a timestamp) must be fully visible above the bottom nav so the complete state is distinguishable from the start state.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"A brown confirmation card visible only as a sliver above the bottom nav, all text hidden\", \"Hero 'Sponsored stream message' in dark ochre on navy, identical to the start screen\", \"'Sponsored by Neighborhood Newsletter' card with Sponsor, Reason, Impression recorded, Layout rows\", \"'Home' highlighted in bottom nav\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can the complete state be distinguished from the start state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Only an untitled brown strip appears above the nav bar; all other content matches the start screen\",\n          \"why\": \"The confirmation card is entirely occluded, leaving no readable difference between the two states.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"b4dd8a3dc58cd1abe478500a2021d48ac678475532308df895554c17019c726d\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"message-stream-evidence-duplicated\",\n      \"title\": \"platform-message-stream reuses platform-messages-entry screenshots and shows invite content at start\",\n      \"description\": \"The message-stream action screenshot is byte-identical to the messages-entry action screenshot (both hash b2b647169c633d36215dcec3936827bc0d27fb369c064bab2ac8dc8c535edc3f) and the message-stream complete screenshot is byte-identical to the messages-entry complete screenshot (both hash 94f3b1d3dabbde57109e81cb83ddff97927cef9596e2056108e646fad9248da5). Both show a single 'Message thread' with 'Maya Chen -> Jordan Lee' and 'Can you bring the sign-in sheets before the meetup?'. The message-stream start screenshot, meanwhile, shows connection-invite content: the heading 'Member connection invite', 'Invite body — Message: \\\"Want to coordinate the Saturday welcome table together?\\\"', and a 'Cancel invite' chip. No screenshot in this row group shows a stream of multiple messages.\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Capture distinct message-stream screenshots showing an actual multi-message stream (several senders, timestamps, read markers) for start, action and complete, and fix the start capture so it opens on stream content rather than the connection-invite surface.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"complete-state-confirmation-clipped\",\n      \"title\": \"Every complete-state screen clips its confirmation card behind the bottom nav\",\n      \"description\": \"The confirmation that distinguishes each complete state is truncated by the Home/Calendar/Admin/Messages bar in all six complete screenshots: 'Banner no-fill recorded / No sponsored message is shown' is cut mid-line; 'Sensitive no-fill recorded' shows only its title row; the in-stream-ad confirmation is reduced to an untitled brown sliver; 'Blocked state confirmed' is cut at 'and appeal/unblock option'; 'Connection invite sent' is cut at 'state, cancel option, and inbox continuation' on both the connections-entry and connection-invite complete screens.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Add bottom padding equal to the nav bar height (or auto-scroll the confirmation into view) so the completion card is fully readable above the navigation bar in every complete state.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"acceptance-criteria-as-ui-copy\",\n      \"title\": \"Requirement/acceptance-criteria prose is rendered as member-facing UI copy\",\n      \"description\": \"Across nearly every screen, body text enumerates what the screen contains instead of being the content: 'Sender, recipient or audience, timestamp, body, and delivery channel are visible.', 'Reply, read/unread, archive, mute, block, draft, or resend actions match the message state.', 'Show sender, protected recipient, attempted invite body, disabled send option, safety reason, appeal/unblock option, and audit timestamp.', 'Review reserved slot behavior, disclosure, no-fill reason, entitlement, receipt, and restore option.', 'Entitlement scope, renewal or expiry, receipt link, restore/manage action, and affected ad slots are visible.' Section subtitles use the same voice ('Show a clear no-sponsored-message state...', 'Show the member why ads are suppressed...').\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-action\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Replace every field-enumeration sentence with the actual data or with short member-facing copy, e.g. render the entitlement status and a receipt link instead of stating that they 'are visible'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"described-but-missing-controls\",\n      \"title\": \"Disabled, appeal, dismiss and manage controls are described in text but never rendered\",\n      \"description\": \"Screens promise controls that do not exist in the pixels. The blocked-target screens name a 'disabled send option' and an 'appeal/unblock option' with no disabled Send button and no appeal affordance anywhere. The ad screens state 'dismiss, report, and manage-ad controls sit inside the stream' and 'restore/manage action ... are visible' with no Dismiss, Report, Manage or Restore button. The message and invite sheets say 'Reply, mute, archive, or block remain available.' and 'choose reply, mute, archive, or block' while rendering none of those controls, and never offer Accept/Decline on the invite surfaces despite showing an 'Accepted' state.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-action\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Render each named control as a real element in its correct state — a visibly disabled Send with inline reason plus a working Appeal/Unblock on the block guard, and Dismiss/Report/Manage ad on the sponsored surfaces.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"reused-generic-thread-actions-block\",\n      \"title\": \"The same generic 'Thread actions' block is reused on workflows where its verbs do not apply\",\n      \"description\": \"An identical 'Thread actions — Read sender, body, timestamp, and choose reply, mute, archive, or block.' card with the same 'Sender and receiver' and 'Conversation state' rows appears on the messages-entry, blocked-target, connections-entry and connection-invite action sheets. On the 'Connection safety guard' sheet it advertises reply and resend on a conversation whose entire premise is that sending is blocked; on the invite sheets it offers thread verbs where accept/decline are needed. Each of these sheets then re-renders its own 'Sender and recipient' and body rows a second time inside that block, duplicating the card above.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-action\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-action\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Give each workflow an action block scoped to its own verbs (accept/decline for invites, appeal/report for blocks) and remove the duplicated sender/body restatement from the lower card.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"repeated-minimized-card-shells\",\n      \"title\": \"Stacked identical minimized card shells with a shared truncated subtitle\",\n      \"description\": \"The start screens stack two and three cards that differ only by title: 'Connections', 'Connection invite' and 'Message stream rend…' each carry the same 'Minimized' chip, the same 'Tap for expanded view' and 'Community setting' chips, the same 'Expand' button, and the byte-identical truncated subtitle 'Member communication stays scoped to the com…'. The 'Message stream rend…' and 'Sensitive page ad sta…' titles are themselves truncated mid-word.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Give each card a distinct, complete subtitle describing its own content, widen or wrap the title so it is not truncated mid-word, and replace the stacked shells with real content rows (conversations, connections, pending requests).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"low-contrast-workflow-hero-titles\",\n      \"title\": \"Workflow hero titles rendered in low-contrast accent tints on the dark panel\",\n      \"description\": \"'Top banner no-fill' (dark green), 'Sensitive page ad guard' (muted purple) and 'Sponsored stream message' (dark ochre) are all drawn against the navy panel at noticeably lower contrast than the white section headings directly below them, with even fainter subtitles. On each screen the workflow's own title is the least legible text on the screen and reads as disabled rather than as a heading.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Lighten the accent tints used for hero titles and subtitles on dark panels so they meet normal on-dark contrast, keeping the accent hue for identity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"wrong-nav-tab-highlighted\",\n      \"title\": \"Calendar tab highlighted on the blocked-connection guard completion screen\",\n      \"description\": \"On platform-blocked-target-complete the bottom navigation shows the 'Calendar' pill filled solid blue while the content is 'Blocked connection guard' / 'Blocked state confirmed'. Every other in-app screen in this set highlights 'Home', so the navigation is asserting a location that contradicts the content.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Keep the navigation selection in sync with the displayed surface so the messaging/safety guard does not render with the Calendar tab active.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"contradictory-state-pairs\",\n      \"title\": \"Complete screens show mutually exclusive states side by side\",\n      \"description\": \"platform-messages-entry-complete and platform-message-stream-complete display 'Today 9:12 AM, unread until opened.' and 'Reply, mute, archive, or block remain available.' immediately above a 'Message sent' confirmation. platform-connection-invite-complete shows a check-icon 'Accepted — Accepted invites open a thread and connection history.' immediately above 'Connection invite sent'. In each case the screen simultaneously reports two states that cannot both be current.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Update the conversation card to reflect the post-action state (read/sent, or sent-and-pending) so the confirmation and the card above it agree.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"start-screens-open-mid-scroll\",\n      \"title\": \"Start states open mid-scroll on clipped headings and orphaned fragments\",\n      \"description\": \"platform-messages-entry-start opens on the orphan sentence 'preserves read/unread receipt.' directly under the app bar, with an 'Archive thread' chip and 'Reply' pill belonging to an invisible thread. platform-connections-entry-start and platform-connection-invite-start both open on a 'Conversation actions' heading sheared to its descenders. In all three the user's first view is a fragment rather than the top of the workflow.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Ensure start states render scrolled to the top of the workflow surface with its title and primary content in view.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"empty-region-on-invite-start\",\n      \"title\": \"Large empty region below the collapsed 'Local package details' row\",\n      \"description\": \"platform-connection-invite-start ends with a collapsed 'Local package details' disclosure row followed by roughly a quarter-screen of blank navy before the bottom navigation, in a start state where an invite composer or recipient list would be expected.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Fill the invite start state with the composer (recipient picker, message field, mutual-community context) so no large dead region remains above the nav bar.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"messages-nav-pill-clipped\",\n      \"title\": \"'Messages' bottom-nav pill sliced by the right screen edge\",\n      \"description\": \"On the majority of in-app screens the fourth navigation pill renders as 'Messages' with its rounded container cut off by the right edge of the viewport, unlike the fully contained Home, Calendar and Admin pills. On a small number of screens (top-banner-no-fill-complete, sensitive-no-fill-complete, in-stream-ad-complete) the row fits, indicating an inconsistent horizontal layout rather than an intentional scrollable nav.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-messages-entry-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-blocked-target-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connections-entry-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-message-stream-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-sensitive-no-fill-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-connection-invite-complete\", \"member-social-space-platform-in-stream-ad-start\", \"member-social-space-platform-top-banner-no-fill-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Constrain the navigation row to the viewport width (or make it explicitly scrollable) so no pill is clipped by the screen edge.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":14148,"ttft_stream_ms":13323,"time_to_request_ms":12339,"type":"result","duration_ms":521978,"uuid":"9611e28f-afe5-462a-91ff-1c1334b2fa91"}
